### name: canon.sort.after-dedupe.postgresql
--- note
DISTINCT keeps the canonical number numeric, so the sort after it is still
numeric.
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("k", CANON(_["n"]))) .> DEDUPE() .> SORT_BY(_["k"])
--- expect
SELECT "_sub1".* FROM (SELECT DISTINCT trim_scale(CAST("n" AS NUMERIC)) AS "k" FROM "r") "_sub1" ORDER BY "_sub1"."k" ASC
===

### name: plan.canon.dedupe-after-a-join.postgresql
--- note
Scenario 6's shape with the rule saying what it means: both DEDUPE fields
compared by value. Without CANON this plan is pure_memory
(plan.identity-barrier.computed-dedupe-after-a-join-stays-local.*); with it,
the whole pipeline is one statement.
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"PRODUCTS":{"kind":"relation","from":"products","fields":{"ID":{"kind":"column","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"CATEGORY_ID":{"kind":"column","column":"category_id","type":"NUM"},"IS_ACTIVE":{"kind":"column","column":"is_active","type":"NUM"}}},"ORDER_ITEMS":{"kind":"relation","from":"order_items","fields":{"ID":{"kind":"column","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"PRODUCT_ID":{"kind":"column","column":"product_id","type":"NUM"}}}}
--- source
PRODUCTS .> LINK_LEFT(ORDER_ITEMS, _["products"]["id"] == _2["product_id"]) .> FILTER(IS_NULL(_["order_items"]["id"])) .> MAP(RECORD("category_id", CANON(_["products"]["category_id"]), "status", CANON(IF(_["products"]["is_active"] == 1, 1, 1.0)))) .> DEDUPE() .> SORT_BY(_["category_id"]) .> TAKE(10)
--- plan
pure_sql
--- tables
products
order_items
--- expect
SELECT "_sub1".* FROM (SELECT DISTINCT trim_scale(CAST("products"."category_id" AS NUMERIC)) AS "category_id", trim_scale(CAST(CASE WHEN ("products"."is_active" = 1) THEN 1 ELSE 1.0 END AS NUMERIC)) AS "status" FROM "products" LEFT JOIN "order_items" "_2" ON ("products"."id" = "_2"."product_id") WHERE (CAST("_2"."id" AS TEXT) IS NULL)) "_sub1" ORDER BY "_sub1"."category_id" ASC LIMIT 10
===

### name: plan.canon.dedupe-after-a-join.mariadb
--- note
On the MySQL family the canonical form is text, so the sort by it runs in
memory; everything before it is one statement.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"PRODUCTS":{"kind":"relation","from":"products","fields":{"ID":{"kind":"column","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"CATEGORY_ID":{"kind":"column","column":"category_id","type":"NUM"},"IS_ACTIVE":{"kind":"column","column":"is_active","type":"NUM"}}},"ORDER_ITEMS":{"kind":"relation","from":"order_items","fields":{"ID":{"kind":"column","column":"id","type":"NUM"},"PRODUCT_ID":{"kind":"column","column":"product_id","type":"NUM"}}}}
--- source
PRODUCTS .> LINK_LEFT(ORDER_ITEMS, _["products"]["id"] == _2["product_id"]) .> FILTER(IS_NULL(_["order_items"]["id"])) .> MAP(RECORD("category_id", CANON(_["products"]["category_id"]), "status", CANON(IF(_["products"]["is_active"] == 1, 1, 1.0)))) .> DEDUPE() .> SORT_BY(_["category_id"]) .> TAKE(10)
--- plan
hybrid
--- tables
products
order_items
--- expect
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(REGEXP_REPLACE(REGEXP_SUBSTR(REGEXP_REPLACE(CAST(`products`.`category_id` AS CHAR), '(?<=^-)0+(?=[0-9])|^0+(?=[0-9])', ''), '^-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]*[1-9])?'), '^-0$', '0') AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin AS `category_id`, CAST(REGEXP_REPLACE(REGEXP_SUBSTR(REGEXP_REPLACE(CAST(CASE WHEN (`products`.`is_active` = 1) THEN 1 ELSE 1.0 END AS CHAR), '(?<=^-)0+(?=[0-9])|^0+(?=[0-9])', ''), '^-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]*[1-9])?'), '^-0$', '0') AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin AS `status` FROM `products` LEFT JOIN `order_items` `_2` ON (`products`.`id` = `_2`.`product_id`) WHERE (`_2`.`id` IS NULL)
===

### name: plan.canon.lets-the-identity-barrier-through.mariadb
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("k", CANON(_["n"] * 1.0 + 0.50))) .> DEDUPE()
--- plan
pure_sql
--- tables
r
--- expect
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(REGEXP_REPLACE(REGEXP_SUBSTR(REGEXP_REPLACE(CAST(((`n` * 1.0) + 0.50) AS CHAR), '(?<=^-)0+(?=[0-9])|^0+(?=[0-9])', ''), '^-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]*[1-9])?'), '^-0$', '0') AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin AS `k` FROM `r`
===

### name: plan.canon.a-computed-field-upstream-is-no-barrier.mariadb
--- note
The canonical form does not depend on how its argument is spelled, so the
barrier does not ask whether the MAP before it kept `x`'s identity: `x` is
computed, and read here through the guard like any undeclared column.
--- dialect
